WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.500
Welcome to Cloud Minute

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:03.700
Today I'm going to show you how to enable and disable APIs

00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:05.300
in the Google Cloud Platform

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:06.966
I'm working on a new project and when I run

00:00:06.966 --> 00:00:08.966
and when I run
'gcloud compute instances list'

00:00:08.966 --> 00:00:11.166
I get an error saying that access is not configured.

00:00:11.566 --> 00:00:12.533
If you run into this

00:00:12.533 --> 00:00:15.366
it just means you haven't enabled that API for your project.

00:00:15.766 --> 00:00:18.166
Google Cloud Platform requires you to enable APIs

00:00:18.166 --> 00:00:20.266
so that you're only using the products you want to use.

00:00:20.833 --> 00:00:23.566
From the Developers Console click APIs &amp; auth

00:00:23.866 --> 00:00:25.333
and then click APIs

00:00:25.966 --> 00:00:28.566
Now you need to select the API you want to enable.

00:00:28.566 --> 00:00:30.266
If it isn't listed on this first page 

00:00:30.266 --> 00:00:32.066
you can search for it using the search box.

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:34.266
Once you find the API you want

00:00:34.266 --> 00:00:37.000
click on the name and then click enable API

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:39.966
Once it finished enabling

00:00:39.966 --> 00:00:43.133
I can use the gcloud compute functions from the command line

00:00:43.833 --> 00:00:46.466
If you want to see what APIs are enabled for your project

00:00:46.466 --> 00:00:49.466
click APIs, Enabled APIs and that will show you a list

00:00:49.466 --> 00:00:51.800
of the APIs currently enabled for your project.

00:00:52.233 --> 00:00:53.466
If you want to disable an API

00:00:53.466 --> 00:00:54.966
you can do so from here or you can do 

00:00:54.966 --> 00:00:57.400
so from the APIs page where you enabled it

00:00:57.700 --> 00:00:58.900
I hope you found this helpful.

